From 8d704e0d420530db0e3cabc4846f8b4a4487e3df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] validation: prepare decoded RPC transaction checks before
 cs_main

Run CheckRegularTransaction and prepare BIP143 sighash data in the RPC
batch decoder's workers before acquiring cs_main. Pass those results to
atomic batch acceptance instead of repeating context-free checks there.
Transaction IDs and raw hashes are already eagerly constructed, so omit
no-op getter warming. The decoder already supplies the parallel loop;
remove the uncalled second parallel helper.

Original-Commit: b4f7c70896f3384050fdad52f884a97513cb2538
Original-Patch: ecash/042

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
Preserve earlier purposeful source repairs through downstream consumer/context adaptations; exact conflict ledger retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.

Coordinator historical decoder recovery (2026-10-21):
Recover persistent bounded shared decoder workers and once-per-tx ID hex reuse. Validate string argument types and preserve earliest malformed index, response order and no partial admission. Use the separately owned utility prerequisite; no staged-admission API dependency. Actual shared normal/focused tests pass, but one explicit OP_TRUE50 pair did not demonstrate speedup.

